  "definition": "Failure to Timely Process Registration Submittal",
  "effectiveDate": "2021-12-21",
  "historyNote": "#13210, INTERIM, eff 6-15-21; ss by #13314, eff 12-21-21",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wt 1004.03",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 1004.03 Failure to Timely Process Registration Submittal",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 1004.03 Failure to Timely Process Registration Submittal.\n\n(a) If the department does not respond within the time period specified in Env-Wt 1004.02, the owner may submit a written request to the department requesting a response.\n\n(b) If the department fails to respond to the request in (a) above within an additional 5 business days, then the following shall apply:\n\n(1) The owner shall be deemed to have submitted a complete and qualifying registration; and\n\n(2) The owner may proceed with the repair or replacement of the legally existing docking structures as presented in the registration filing.\n\n(c) A valid registration issued pursuant to Env-Wt 1004.02 or granted pursuant to Env-Wt 1004.03 shall not relieve the owner of any obligation to comply with all requirements applicable to the project, including but not limited to requirements established in or under RSA 482-A and RSA 485-A relative to water quality.\n\nSource. #13210, INTERIM, eff 6-15-21; ss by #13314, eff 12-21-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt1000.html"
}
